.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
# Ignore all fetched/generated data. Regeneration steps live in skill/data-process.md;
# what the data actually is lives in doc/data.md.
# Leading slash matters: a bare `data/` also matches src/data/, which is SOURCE CODE
# (the crawlers) and must stay tracked.
/data/
# dashboard/data.js is committed so the dashboard works from a fresh clone
# (data/ contents are ignored, so they can't be regenerated after cloning)

# Standalone replays (dashboard/replay_<year>_<loc>.html) ARE committed: they are the
# only replay you can open by double-clicking, since the data is inlined and the page
# has no external references at all. replay.html, the picker, fetches its payload and
# so needs a server — see skill/dashboard.md.
#
# The cost is deliberate: each is ~3 MB of generated content and git keeps every
# revision, so rebuilding the same race repeatedly grows the repo permanently. Commit
# the races you actually want a clone to have, not every experiment.
dashboard/replays/

# Local Claude Code settings (worktrees, per-machine overrides)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
